mGBA runs a DMA one unit (16 or 32 bits) per timing event, ~2000 per frame in Pokemon games,
each re-picking the DMA and rescheduling its event. While a DMA between plain memory is due and
nothing else is, its middle units now run back to back, rescheduling once at the end: same
loads, stores, cycles and event times (tools/mgba_exact.sh: identical to pristine mGBA over
280K+ frames of 6 games). mTimingTick re-reads the clock, which the DMA event now advances.

